---
title: Maple Bubble Bread
servings: 20
cookTime: 40 minutes
totalTime: 70 minutes
source.name: Taste of Home
source.url: http://www.tasteofhome.com/recipes/Maple-Bubble-Bread
tags: Desserts
---

= Dough =
In a #large bowl{}, dissolve @active dry yeast{1/4%oz} in @water{1/4%cup}(warm, 110°F to 115°F).

Add the @milk{1%cup}(2% fat, warm, 110°F to 115°F), @butter{1/3%cup}(melted), @sugar{1/4%cup},
@egg{1}, @egg yolk{1}, @salt{1/2%tsp}, and @all-purpose flour{3%cups}.
Beat on medium speed for ~{3%minutes}. 

Stir in enough remaining @all-purpose flour{2%cups}(as needed) to form a firm dough.

Turn onto a floured surface; knead until smooth and elastic, about ~{6-8%minutes}.

Place in a greased bowl, turning once to grease the top.
Cover and let rise in a warm place until doubled, about ~{1%hour}.

= Topping =
In a small saucepan, combine @maple syrup{2/3%cup} and @butter{2%tbsp}. 
Bring to a boil. Cook and stir for ~{3%minutes}; set aside.

Punch dough down. Turn onto a lightly floured surface; divide into 20 pieces.
Shape each into a roll. 

In a shallow bowl, combine @brown sugar{1%cup}(packed) and @ground cinnamon{1/2%tsp}.
Place @butter{3%tbsp}(melted) in a separate shallow bowl. 

Dip buns in butter, then coat in brown sugar mixture.

Place eight rolls in a greased 10-in. #fluted tube pan{}; drizzle with 1/3 cup syrup mixture.
Top with remaining rolls, syrup and brown sugar mixture.

Cover and let rise until doubled, about ~{45%minutes}.

While rising, preheat oven to 350°F.
Bake for ~{30-35%minutes} or until golden brown.

Cool for ~{10%minutes} before inverting onto a serving plate. Serve warm.
